WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.475
Chapter 06 makes the address plan
the join key for the evidence.

2
00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:08.525
A scan tells you what answered; the
IPAM tells you what was allocated.

3
00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:12.035
So every inventory reconciles against it,

4
00:00:12.035 --> 00:00:17.650
and BOD 23-01 already asks for
automated discovery every seven days.

5
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.225
In Azure, the enterprise
IPAM stays the authority.

6
00:00:21.225 --> 00:00:26.079
Reserve the block there first, mirror
it into Virtual Network Manager pools,

7
00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:30.316
then use policy to deny any virtual
network without an allocation,

8
00:00:30.316 --> 00:00:32.088
and reconcile by discovery.

9
00:00:32.088 --> 00:00:36.630
Virtual Network Manager isn't named
in Microsoft's FedRAMP audit scope,

10
00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:40.249
so record it as a dependency
until coverage is confirmed.

11
00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:45.650
The book builds all this as layered modules,
each writing its state as evidence.

12
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.628
And it treats outside inputs as code too,

13
00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:53.050
like the monthly Microsoft
endpoint list a GCC tenant uses.

14
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.700
Next, the front door.
